 triage:id "REQ-C1-001" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-command/src/envelope.rs:244; crates/sc-command/src/error.rs:436; crates/sc-command/src/error.rs:441" ;
 triage:issue "New public command schema trait implementations contain expect calls. The binding banned-construct rule explicitly rejects invariant/comment justifications; the existing Noop literal exception does not cover schema conversion." ;
 triage:action "Construct canonical schemas with infallible native schema APIs, preserving exact Envelope/OpError wire shape and both schema engines; verify no new public-path banned constructs remain. The adapter schema expects at contract.rs:321/333 also warrant the same owner-schema repair rather than a panic-policy waiver." ;
 triage:disposition "Infallible native Schemars/Utoipa schemas in sc-command envelope/error and sc-cron-commands contract; six schema-enabled contract regressions, including exact arbitrary-JSON wire checks." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .

triage:C1_QA1_REQ_C1_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C1-002" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs:9; crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs:76; crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs:128; crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs:159; crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs:183" ;
 triage:issue "The new request/target/environment DTOs derive Debug over payloads, Python module/Monty source and Set/Reference strings. Formatting a normal CronRequest/StartRequest diagnostically exposes the sensitive values that the contract prohibits in diagnostics, unlike the core environment model's value-free Debug." ;
 triage:action "Provide value-free Debug implementations for sensitive DTOs and nested variants, retaining names/kinds/counts where safe; add canary tests through complete CronRequest/StartRequest formatting, without changing intentional raw wire serialization." ;
 triage:disposition "Value-free sensitive leaf and aggregate Debug in sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs; nested source/payload/environment/reference canary and unchanged serialization tests." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .

triage:C1_QA1_REQ_C1_003 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C1-003" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs:307; crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs:315; examples/spike/phase-c-contract/composition/src/main.rs:10" ;
 triage:issue "CronRequest JsonSchema has oneOf but no root type:object. The temporary probe only declares Option<Parameters<CronRequest>> and does not exercise actual RMCP tool-schema construction. The actual C3 projection failure reports that this owner schema is invalid for RMCP inputSchema; C6's narrow fix is not present at reviewed 030f9ed." ;
 triage:action "Backport the canonical JsonSchema-only object-root repair and regression (a952ed2 or equivalent), preserving the Utoipa oneOf typed variants; verify actual RMCP tool construction, not only an Option type declaration. Do not add type:object to the shared OpenAPI conversion if that erases its oneOf." ;
 triage:disposition "CronRequest JsonSchema-only object root; actual rmcp3.8 schema_for_input and Tool construction in tests/contracts/phase-c/application-control; typed Utoipa oneOf remains separate." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .

triage:C1_QA1_REQ_C1_004 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C1-004" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/src/consumer_contract.rs:15; crates/sc-cron/src/consumer_contract.rs:79; docs/plans/phase-c/compatibility-contract.md:529" ;
 triage:issue "The supported custom CronOperations path cannot supply the StoreOperationContext required by StandardCronExecutor::new in an ordinary downstream build. Context fields are private and its only factory at this C1 snapshot is operation_context_probe behind test-utils; no normal constructor/default or standalone owner factory is declared. Requiring a framework worker or a test feature defeats the documented own-lifecycle replacement path." ;
 triage:action "Freeze and supply a narrow normal public context/owner creation seam suitable for custom operations and document its cancellation/deadline/ownership responsibilities. Add a normal-only external consumer composition proof with custom CronOperations, without enabling test-utils or starting a bundled worker. Production Scheduler/executor behavior remains C5/C6 work." ;
 triage:disposition "Normal WorkerStopControl::new and finish_application_shutdown in application_control.rs; external ordinary-feature custom provider proves earliest deadline, shared cancellation, ordinary-thread stop and revocation after acknowledgement with future grace. Contract documents application join responsibility and later framework restriction." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .

