triage:C1_QA1_ARCH_C1_003 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "ARCH-C1-003" ;
 triage:severity "BLOCKING" ;
 triage:reviewer "arch-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs" ;
 triage:issue "EnvironmentOperation derives Debug over Set(String) and Reference(String); the containing EnvironmentPolicy, StartRequest, CronOperation and CronRequest propagate those raw fields. ExecutionTarget also derives Debug over Monty source/Python module and StartRequest includes arbitrary payload. This newly shared wire model creates value-bearing diagnostic formatting rather than the value-free environment-model behavior required by ADR0016 points6/8." ;
 triage:action "Give sensitive leaf/aggregate DTOs value-free Debug implementations or remove unsupported Debug derivations, preserving serde/schema behavior. Add a diagnostic canary proving plaintext values, locators, source, payload and sensitive paths do not appear." ;
 triage:disposition "Value-free sensitive leaf and aggregate Debug in sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs; nested source/payload/environment/reference canary and unchanged serialization tests." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .

triage:C1_QA1_ARCH_C1_004 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "ARCH-C1-004" ;
 triage:severity "BLOCKING" ;
 triage:reviewer "arch-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "docs/plans/phase-c/compatibility-contract.md" ;
 triage:issue "The frozen StandardCronExecutor constructor requires StoreOperationContext, but the shared context has private fields and C1 offers no ordinary public root construction/control contract. The sole worker-free constructor operation_context_probe is test-utils-gated (consumer_contract.rs82). The same contract advertises custom CronOperations for application-owned schema/shutdown at lines116-125, while ADR-CRNC0001 explicitly forbids hidden concrete-Scheduler/private wiring as a replacement for those ports. A custom provider cannot compose the promised narrower override through normal APIs." ;
 triage:action "Freeze a minimal supported production context-creation/cancellation-ownership seam for application-owned CronOperations, without a dummy Scheduler worker or test-utils. Preserve shared live cancellation and earliest-deadline semantics and add a normal-feature external composition proof. C1 owns the usable contract; this finding does not demand the later C5/C6 implementation bodies here." ;
 triage:disposition "Normal WorkerStopControl::new and finish_application_shutdown in application_control.rs; external ordinary-feature custom provider proves earliest deadline, shared cancellation, ordinary-thread stop and revocation after acknowledgement with future grace. Contract documents application join responsibility and later framework restriction." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .

