triage:C1_QA1_FTQ_C1_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C1-001" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "examples/spike/phase-c-contract/probe.py" ;
 triage:issue "Retained executable qualification probes call subprocess.run with captured stdout/stderr and no execution deadline or owned-tree cleanup. Cargo can wait indefinitely on a registry/artifact lock or a stalled tool; a surviving descendant can retain a capture pipe. The probe then never fails or reclaims its command tree. selective_probe.py:32 and probe.py:55 repeat the same mechanism." ;
 triage:action "Complete the sprint's already-required temporary-probe retirement before merge. If any qualification executable is deliberately retained, route every command through the existing bounded owned-process helper with a hard failure guard and physical cleanup; do not add retries or a new evidence mechanism." ;
 triage:disposition "Removed entire examples/spike/phase-c-contract tree. Concise current qualification closeout belongs in existing PR116 body; actual frozen ADR results retained. Durable consumer uses canonical bounded owned_process.run." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .

triage:C1_QA1_FTQ_C1_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C1-002" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child_windows.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The normal-completion BEFORE observation still depends on the inner Python owner's weaker completion rule. For a nonexpired bridge, output invokes completed() before the strong outer Bridge::stop. The inner _terminate_windows_job returns as soon as ActiveProcesses is zero, which need not mean descendant process handles are signaled. A descendant can therefore remain unsignaled after the Python bridge exits and make the immediate BEFORE assertion fail, even though the outer retained-identity cleanup would subsequently finish it. The stronger outer owner at this revision does not protect that earlier observation boundary." ;
 triage:action "Promote the shared Python owned-process retained-identity completion repair to this branch, so the inner owner establishes physical signaling before returning. Keep the immediate BEFORE observation and its distinction from emergency cleanup; do not move it after outer cleanup or pad the observer wait. Add/retain a deterministic empty-job-before-unsignaled-identity negative and actual Windows proof for the resulting source." ;
 triage:disposition "Promoted retained physical-process identity completion before canonical Python owner returns, plus deterministic active-empty/unsignaled negative and immediate witnesses. Shared helper source compared against C5 native-Windows validated source; macOS is not represented as Windows proof." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .

triage:C1_QA1_FTQ_C1_003 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C1-003" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented-pending-reqa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "030f9ed16edf70a6f51e20905c5ab292c2d6389c" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child_unix.py" ;
 triage:issue "The new Unix bridge calls canonical _launch directly without the canonical Unix inspection preflight. If ps is unavailable, it can launch target/descendant work in separate process groups and only discover the missing cleanup capability when the stop inspector runs. That inspector fails; Session::stop returns an error and Drop falls back to killing only the leader's process group. Distinct-group descendants used by this fixture are then left alive. The error is reported, but ownership has already been lost." ;
 triage:action "Refuse launch before creating target work when required session inspection is unavailable, reusing the existing _check_session_inspection mechanism under the supervisor environment. Cover the unsupported-inspection path causally and ensure any cleanup-failure fallback does not discard already-known cross-group work; retain the bounded cleanup budget and physical ownership rather than silently claiming success." ;
 triage:disposition "Canonical bridge performs session-inspection preflight before target launch; negative no-launch test retained. Canonical owned_process test suite passes10 tests on macOS." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/116#issuecomment-6648238015" .
